# Paper D, track T5: certificate data

Brackets `[pl/q, ph/q]` of the crossing `ε_N` with `q = 2^64`, and a reference index `b₀`, for
`N = 5, …, 400`. For `N ≥ 10` the brackets are the enclosures `eps_lo`, `eps_hi` of
`paperD/data/witnesses_convex_2026-10-17.jsonl` (written by `certify_convex.py`), rounded outward
to the denominator `2^64`. For `5 ≤ N ≤ 9` they come from a bisection in exact rational
arithmetic (40 steps from `[1/100, 49/100]`), also rounded outward. `b₀` is the index with the
largest lower end of the enclosure (the checker is sound for every `b₀`). None of these numbers
is trusted: the checker in `PaperD.T5_Checker` validates each of them.

Each list `convexData_a_b` holds the triples `(pl, ph, b₀)` for `N = a, a+1, …, b`, and each list
`centerData_a_b` the triples for the even `N = a, a+2, …, b`.
-/

